-- title:
--   q-expansion principle for X₀(ℓ), ℓ prime
-- statement:
--   Let $\ell$ be a prime, let $f, g$ be formal Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$ and let $F \colon \mathfrak{H} \to \mathbb{C}$ be a function on the upper half-plane. Assume: (hF) for every $\tau \in \mathfrak{H}$ the family $m \mapsto f_m \, q_1(\tau)^m$, indexed by $m \in \mathbb{Z}$, with $f_m$ the $m$-th coefficient of $f$ viewed in $\mathbb{C}$ and $q_h(\tau) = \exp(2\pi i \tau / h)$ (`Function.Periodic.qParam`), is summable with sum $F(\tau)$; (hG) for every $\tau$ the family $m \mapsto g_m \, q_\ell(\tau)^m$ is summable with sum $F(S \cdot \tau)$, where $S = \begin{pmatrix} 0 & -1 \\ 1 & 0\end{pmatrix}$ acts by fractional linear transformations; and (hinv) $F(\gamma \cdot \tau) = F(\tau)$ for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(\ell)$ and every $\tau$. Then $f$ lies in [`ModularCurve.modularFunctionField ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L250), the intermediate field of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ generated by the two elements [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) and [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ ℓ ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25); here [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157) is the series whose realisation at period $1$ is $E_4^3/\Delta$, and [`ModularCurve.qExpand ℚ ℓ`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L25) is the ring endomorphism of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ multiplying all exponents by $\ell$, i.e. $q \mapsto q^\ell$. Thus $f \in \mathbb{Q}(j(q), j(q^\ell))$.
--
--   This is the $q$-expansion principle for the modular curve $X_0(\ell)$ with $\ell$ prime: a $\Gamma_0(\ell)$-invariant function on the upper half-plane whose expansions at the two cusps (period $1$ at $\infty$, period $\ell$ at $0$) have rational coefficients has its expansion at $\infty$ in the function field $\mathbb{Q}(j(q), j(q^\ell))$ of $X_0(\ell)$. It is used to place the $q$-expansions of modular units on $X_0(\ell)$ inside that field, via [`ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.modularUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionField) and [`ModularCurve.sharpUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionField`](thm.html#ModularCurve.sharpUnitSeries_mem_modularFunctionField).
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_mem_modularFunctionField_of_hasSum_of_gamma0_invariant.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_X0
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.Exp
import Mathlib.Analysis.Complex.UpperHalfPlane.MoebiusAction
